['Here's a basic outline of how you can write this Java program using Java 8 features like Streams and CompletableFutures for concurrency management. This code is not complete, but it should give you a good starting point for your task:

```java
import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.image.BufferedImage;
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import javax.imageio.ImageIO;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class ImageConverter {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(ImageConverter.class.getName());
    private ExecutorService executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors());

    public void convertImagesInDirectory(String directory, String sourceFormat, String targetFormat) {
        try (Stream<Path> paths = Files.walk(Paths.get(directory))) {
            paths
                .filter(Files::isRegularFile)
                .map(Path::toString)
                .forEach(file -> executorService.submit(() -> {
                    File sourceImageFile = new File(file);
                    if (sourceImageFile.getName().endsWith("." + sourceFormat)) {
                        try {
                            BufferedImage bufferedImage = ImageIO.read(sourceImageFile);
                            File targetImageFile = new File(file.replaceAll(sourceFormat + "$", targetFormat));
                            if (targetImageFile.exists()) {
                                Files.delete(targetImageFile.toPath());
                            }
                            ImageIO.write(bufferedImage, targetFormat, targetImageFile);
                            Files.delete(sourceImageFile.toPath());
                            logger.info("Converted image: " + sourceImageFile.getName() + " to format: " + targetFormat);
                        } catch (IOException e) {
                            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to convert image: " + file, e);
                        }
                    }
                }));
        } catch (IOException e) {
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Error while accessing directory: " + directory, e);
        } finally {
            executorService.shutdown();
        }
    }
}
```

This code uses the Executors framework to create a thread pool and submits tasks (image conversions) to this pool. Conversion results are logged using Java's built-in logging facility. This program also handles IOExceptions by catching them in the CompletableFuture tasks, logging error details and then swallowing the exception to prevent it from propagating further.

Note: This is a simplified example that assumes you can convert all images in a given directory to the same target format. In a real-world scenario, this would likely involve more complex logic (e.g., determining the correct source format based on file extension, handling different directories with varying formats etc.) and would also require proper error handling for edge cases like network failures or missing files.
']

