['Here's a basic implementation for your requirements in JavaScript, which uses fetch API to interact with external CMS API:

```javascript
// predefined list of allowed HTML tags and attributes
const ALLOWED_TAGS = {
  'script': [], // no attributes required. can be extended as per the needs
};

function escapeHtml(text) {
  return text
    .replace(/&/g, "&amp;")
    .replace(/</g, "&lt;")
    .replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
}

async function createFooterScriptTags(arrayOfScriptObjects = [], minify = false, lazyLoad = true) {
  const footerElement = document.getElementById('footer');

  if (!arrayOfScriptObjects.length) {
    console.log("No scripts found.");

    // Fetch scripts from CMS API in case array is empty
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/api/scripts', /* options */);
      arrayOfScriptObjects = await response.json();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Failed to get scripts: ', err);
      return;
    }
  }

  for (let scriptObj of arrayOfScriptObjects) {
    if (!scriptObj || !ALLOWED_TAGS[scriptObj.tagName]) continue; // Invalid script object

    let scriptTag = `<${scriptObj.tagName} id="${escapeHtml(scriptObj.id)}" title="${escapeHtml(scriptObj.title)}">${minify ? escapeHtml(scriptObj.body) : scriptObj.body}</${scriptObj.tagName}>`;

    if (lazyLoad) {
      scriptTag = scriptTag.replace('>', ' async defer>'); // Adding attributes for lazy loading
    }

    footerElement.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", scriptTag);
  }
}
```
This example assumes that the CMS API endpoint is /api/scripts and options are not specified. The function will console log when no scripts found or failed to get scripts from CMS API. You may need to adjust this according to your specific requirements, such as handling script tags with attributes, handling invalid HTML in body etc.

The above code does not include lazy loading optimization techniques such as Intersection Observer API for efficient resource allocation and handling network latency issues. Also, the footer tag should be present in the DOM before running this function to avoid errors.

