```javascript
app.service('RefreshService', ['$http', '$q', function($http, $q) {
    var activeRequests = {}; // tracks active requests per field

    this.refreshField = function(resourceId, url, fieldName) {
        if (activeRequests[fieldName]) return activeRequests[fieldName];

        var deferred = $q.defer();
        activeRequests[fieldName] = deferred.promise;

        // send the refresh message to parent window
        parent.postMessage({ type: 'refresh', field: fieldName }, '*');

        // start refreshing with 3 attempts
        var attempt = 1, maxAttempts = 3;
        function tryRefresh() {
            return $http.get(url + '/' + resourceId)
                .then(function successCallback(response) {
                    if (!response || !response.data) {
                        deferred.reject('Empty response from server');
                    } else {
                        // assuming the field value is in response.data[fieldName]
                        var result = response.data[fieldName];

                        // send a message to parent window with the refresh result
                        parent.postMessage({ type: 'refreshResult', field: fieldName, data: result }, '*');

                        deferred.resolve(result);
                    }
                })
                .catch(function errorCallback(error) {
                    if (attempt < maxAttempts) {
                        attempt++;
                        tryRefresh();
                    } else {
                        deferred.reject('Failed to refresh after ' + attempt + ' attempts');
                    }
                });
        }

        // start the first attempt
        tryRefresh();

        return deferred.promise;
    };
}]);
```

This `RefreshService` includes retry logic for failed refresh operations, but it doesn't maintain a queue of pending requests per field, which can be added to handle concurrent refresh triggers efficiently. This can help prevent redundant requests and maintain UI responsiveness. However, in this case, we ensure that no more than one refresh request is active per field at any given time by keeping track of all active requests in `activeRequests` object.

