4. Balanced trees can be used to reduce time complexity of node lookup while increasing memory consumption.

To mitigate potential bottlenecks:
1. Implement a cache to store frequently accessed external metadata and update it asynchronously to reduce the impact of frequent updates on traversal speed.
2. Optimize your data structure for fast lookups by children, parent pointers or other relevant parameters.
3. Monitor system performance and adjust allocation strategies accordingly.

