["Here is an example of how this might be accomplished using PHP. This code block demonstrates the concept of modular functions but does not include all the required details. Implementing it in a production environment will require additional work and error handling strategies. 

```php
class UserService {
    private $authService;
    private $dbHandler;
    private $logger;
    private $cacheLayer;
    private $traceSystem;
    private $resourceManager;

    function __construct(AuthServiceInterface $authService, DBHandlerInterface $dbHandler, LoggerInterface $logger, CacheLayerInterface $cacheLayer, TraceSystemInterface $traceSystem, ResourceManagerInterface $resourceManager) {
        $this->authService = $authService;
        $this->dbHandler = $dbHandler;
        $this->logger = $logger;
        $this->cacheLayer = $cacheLayer;
        $this->traceSystem = $traceSystem;
        $this->resourceManager = $resourceManager;
    }

    public function updateUserPassword($userId, $newPassword) {
        $span = $this->traceSystem->startSpan('update_password');

        // Check if data is cached. If it isn't then fetch from DB
        $userData = $this->cacheLayer->get('user_data_'.$userId);
        if (empty($userData)) {
            $userData = $this->dbHandler->fetchUserById($userId);
        }

        // Check external auth service for identity verification
        $verificationResult = $this->authService->verifyIdentity();
        if (!$verificationResult) {
            $span->logError('Failed to verify user identity');
            return false;
        }

        // Acquire lock to prevent race condition and update password
        $lockKey = 'update_password_'.$userId;
        $this->resourceManager->acquireLock($lockKey);
        $updated = $this->dbHandler->updateUserPassword($userData, $newPassword);
        if ($updated) {
            $this->cacheLayer->delete('user_data_'.$userId); // Invalidate cached data after update
        } else {
            $span->logError('Failed to update user password');
        }
        $this->resourceManager->releaseLock($lockKey);

        $this->logger->info('Password updated', ['timestamp' => time()]); // Log password update attempt

        $span->finish();

        return $updated;
    }
}
```
In this example, the class `UserService` integrates with external dependencies (like an authentication service and a distributed tracing system) through interfaces. This allows for flexibility in testing by injecting mocked objects, or changing implementations under different circumstances without having to change the core logic of the function itself. 

