            }, function errorCallback(response) {
                console.log(`Failed to refresh ${fieldName} due to: `, response);

                // Retry logic in case of failure 
                setTimeout(() => refreshDialogFields([fieldName], timeout), 500);
            });
        } else {
            console.log('Field was not refreshed as it does not exist');
        }
    });

    return successCount;
}
```

This function uses a list of field names and a custom timeout for each request. It iterates over the fields, checking if they exist in `window` object (which represents the dialog) before sending an HTTP GET request to a server-side API endpoint based on the field's ID. The responses are handled using Promise, with success being logged and counted separately, while failures triggering retry logic.

