    return (Config){ .numRanges = 1, .ranges = malloc(sizeof(Range)) };
}

float DynamicValueGenerator(Config *config) {
    srand((unsigned int)time(NULL)); // Initialize the random number generator

    if (!config || config->numRanges == 0) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Invalid configuration\n");
        return NAN;
    }

    Range range = config->ranges[rand() % config->numRanges]; // Randomly select a range

    if (range.min > range.max) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Invalid range: min value is greater than max\n");
        return NAN;
    }

    float randomValue = ((float)rand()/(float)(RAND_MAX)) * (range.max - range.min) + range.min; // Generate a random number within the selected range

    return randomValue;
}
```
This function generates a random floating-point number within a pre-defined range, using dynamic memory allocation to store and manage configuration data. The `fetchConfig` function is a placeholder for fetching actual configuration data from an external source. In a real-world application, you would replace this with appropriate code to fetch the configuration data.
